From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: The azahar-nano switches on Linux, Mali found as on Android

azahar-nano reads its switches from Android properties
(persist.gammaos.azahar_nano.<name>, sys.gammaos...) through
<sys/system_properties.h>, which Linux does not have, and turns most of them
on only when it finds a Mali GPU, a check made for Android only.

- darkos/linux/sys/system_properties.h stands in for the Android header: a
  property is the environment variable named like it with dots as
  underscores (persist_gammaos_azahar_nano_fastmem=0), unset reads empty as
  an unset property does, so every switch keeps its default;
- IsMaliDevice() and TweakEnabled() work on Linux too: /dev/mali0 and no
  kgsl node, as on Android. The real-time emulation thread (emu_rt) stays
  Android only.

